{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:40ce13e26f2357d1","name":"Flash Flood","source":{"id":"source:reference-40ce13e26f2357d1","title":"Flash Flood","revision":21325,"timestamp":"2024-08-26T01:35:26Z","sha256":"59b53f1b3caca91d958f1a6b7c07e7369b2f0c60af08c2372e11acfa9c599b7e","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=21325","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=Flash%20Flood&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-40ce13e26f2357d1","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Unknown Regions Campaign Guide"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Unknown_Regions_Campaign_Guide"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Water begins to trickle across the ground slowly, then grows into a rush as flood waters push their way across the ground at breakneck pace."]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["The nature of the landscape on ",{"tag":"a","children":["Volik"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Volik","referenceId":"reference:24aae6e1e2447b18"}," lends itself to Flash Floods. While most of the time this does no more harm than washing away some hidden cache of weapon and contraband, in the right spot a Flash Flood can turn a once-dry plain into a quick-flowing river in a matter of seconds. Gamemasters can use the Hazard to represent Flash Floods that spring up when the heroes are engaged in a combat encounter. The area of the Flash Flood can start small and grow over time, or the entire area of the battlefield could be subjected to the Flash Flood Hazard.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["Flash Flood Statistics (CL 7)"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Keywords:"]}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Natural"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Natural"},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Trigger:"]}," The encounter begins, or a predetermined round number begins (Gamemaster's choice)\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Attack:"]}," +7 vs ",{"tag":"a","children":["Reflex Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Reflex_Defense"},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Damage:"]}," 1d6 and knocked ",{"tag":"a","children":["Prone"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Prone","referenceId":"reference:4d99dff1fb964110"},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Recurrence:"]}," Each Round on ",{"tag":"a","children":["Initiative Count"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Initiative_Count"}," (",{"tag":"a","children":["Initiative"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Initiative","referenceId":"reference:3e687de48a6ad4e5"}," +8) for 10 Rounds\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Suggested ",{"tag":"a","children":["Skills"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Skills","referenceId":"reference:66d0f523a379b2de"},":"]}," The following are suggested ",{"tag":"a","children":["Skills"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Skills","referenceId":"reference:66d0f523a379b2de"}," for this Hazard:\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"ul","children":[{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Acrobatics"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Acrobatics","referenceId":"reference:0d0b7eee2953750e"}," (DC 22):"]}," As a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Reaction"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Reaction"}," to being hit by this Hazard's attack, the character can make an ",{"tag":"a","children":["Acrobatics"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Acrobatics","referenceId":"reference:0d0b7eee2953750e"}," check to keep from being knocked ",{"tag":"a","children":["Prone"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Prone","referenceId":"reference:4d99dff1fb964110"},"."]},"\n",{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Knowledge (Physical Sciences)"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Knowledge_(Physical_Sciences)"}," (DC 17):"]}," The character recognizes the area as one susceptible to flash flooding."]},"\n",{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Swim"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Swim","referenceId":"reference:dd4fa375c70c4e42"}," (DC 17):"]}," The character makes this check as a part of a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Move Action"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Move_Action"},", and if successful can ",{"tag":"a","children":["Swim"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Swim","referenceId":"reference:dd4fa375c70c4e42"}," as normal in the flooded area (this skill can only be used after five rounds of flooding)."]}]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Special:"]}," Each round that it attacks after the first round, the Flash Flood gains a cumulative +1 bonus to its attack rolls. After three rounds, the water is rushing into the area at knee height to a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Human"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Human","referenceId":"reference:9ffa865f2bc6e850"},"; after five rounds, the water is at waist height; and after ten rounds the water is higher than an average Human's head. After ten rounds, the area is effectively flooded, and Gamemasters can either allow heroes to ",{"tag":"a","children":["Swim"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Swim","referenceId":"reference:dd4fa375c70c4e42"}," as normal or use the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Flooded River"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Flooded_River","referenceId":"reference:f1f27197b00860e6"}," Hazard.\n"]},"\n","\n","\n","\n\n","\n\n","\n"]}}
